## Outcome and conditions

Convert cents and fractional quotations, calculate tick values and signed long/short cumulative payoff with total contract exposure, and justify maximum-loss claims from explicit price bounds. Interpret zero crossing and slope as trading P/L rather than account balance. Assume fixed N and q and ignore settlement-flow interest; a maturity use of spot additionally assumes $F_T=S_T$.

Finished-note locations: [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Spot_Forward_and_Futures_Contracts.md#Standardized futures specifications]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Margins_and_Marking_to_Market.md#Daily profit and loss, with units]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Margins_and_Marking_to_Market.md#Payoff and the size of possible losses]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Introduction_to_Futures_Seminar_Exercises.md#Problem 3: copper and maximum loss]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Introduction_to_Futures_Seminar_Exercises.md#The seminar's film illustration]].

